# aether-unified-immutability-model

Aether enforces immutability consistently at three orthogonal levels that together form a coherent model: (1) Binding-level — the `#` sigil marks an identifier as immutable; its referenced object can never be rebound after initialization. (2) Type-level — numeric types (Drop, Mist) are always immutable objects regardless of their binding sigil; the value of a numeric object never changes after creation. (3) Container-level — an immutable container bound with `#` preserves its set of contained references, even if a contained mutable object's internal state later changes. This shallow-immutability-at-reference contract is consistent across all three levels. A common mistake is to conflate binding-immutability with deep-freeze; Aether's model is deliberately shallow at the container level.

## Procedures
- Apply the # sigil to any identifier that must not be rebound after initialization.
- Treat Drop and Mist values as always-immutable regardless of sigil — numeric mutation is impossible.
- When reasoning about whether a #-bound container has 'changed', check whether its reference-set changed, NOT whether any contained mutable object's internal state changed.

## Conventions
- Immutability in Aether is shallow (reference-set) at the container level but absolute for numeric primitives.
- The # sigil documents intent AND enforces rebinding prevention; it does not deep-freeze contained objects.

